WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.816
{\an8}Do you remember working with
any Russian specialists?

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.376
Sorry. what's this about?

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.856
Any progress on our mole?

4
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.816
Sifting through the hay
piece by piece.

5
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.856
There's nothing like going through
your whole love life

6
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.336
with your husband's best friend.
THEY LAUGH.

7
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.776
No tall. dark strangers
taking me aside.

8
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.216
Anything new. or unusual?

9
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.536
From China? Not that I'm aware of.

10
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.256
If they were after something.
what might that be?

11
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.416
And it's definitely
linked to Phil Draper?

12
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.480
Sorry. I forgot my smart card.

13
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.040
David. Charlie's found the mole.

14
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

15
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.216
I was born and grew up in Hong Kong.

16
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.296
My father was a biochemist
and academic at HKU.

17
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.400
My mother...

18
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.120
she enjoyed the expat life...

19
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.576
though I've never truly understood
why Brits are expats

20
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.216
when the rest of the world
are immigrants.

21
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.920
When I was 12.
my father got a post at Bristol.

22
00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.240
We went home...

23
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.296
or should I say
the opposite of home?

24
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.640
What is that? CLICKS TONGUE.

25
00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.480
How did that make you feel?

26
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.400
How did I feel?

27
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.080
Like I'd lost part of myself.

28
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.880
At university. you had
a relationship with a Nicky Chan?

29
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.680
You already know this
and it's in my DV form.

30
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.056
{\an8}BARBARA SIGHS.

31
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.240
{\an8}BARBARA CLEARS THROAT.

32
00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.816
University. Hong Kong.

33
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.096
He was a law postgrad.

34
00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.136
I was at Oxford studying Mandarin.

35
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.720
It was my year abroad.

36
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.960
It was 1997.

37
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.816
I wanted to be there
for the handover.

38
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.000
Historical moment.

39
00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.840
Historical betrayal.

40
00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.616
200 years. our military
and trading post. our friends.

41
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.040
then our government abandons them
to the Chinese Communist Party.

42
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:12.080
Nicky was a student leader.
fiercely opposed to Chinese rule.

43
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.216
Before you ask. I loved him.

44
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.016
And then. one day.
he doesn't show up for a date.

45
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.376
doesn't answer his phone.

46
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.440
I write him letters - nothing.

47
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.880
Had he been arrested?

48
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.080
At first. I was terrified
that he had been...

49
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:33.216
but then I heard from others

50
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.360
he'd joined another
pro-democracy group to avoid me.

51
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.200
Paying me back for our
"historical betrayal". I'm guessing.

52
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.976
BARBARA SIGHS

53
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.896
My relationship with Nicky

54
00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.520
was bound up with my passion
for Hong Kong and the politics.

55
00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:52.760
You know. I...

56
00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.120
It was years ago.

57
00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.960
And have you seen
Mr Chan since 1997?

58
00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.960
In the course of my
duties for MI6. yes.

59
00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.200
We had a leak.

60
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.296
MI6 believed someone had infiltrated

61
00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.040
the anti-Beijing group
we supported...

62
00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.800
a CCP agent.

63
00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.136
I was sent to Hong Kong to find them.

64
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.160
PHONE RINGS

65
00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.696
Well...? How did it go?

66
00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.056
Mark called me himself
straight afterwards.

67
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.896
What. Mark as in
Director of GCHQ? Mm-hm.

68
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.216
He offered me the post -

69
00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.720
Deputy Director of Operations.
You're joking.

70
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.656
Well. that's great! Danny. well done!

71
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.016
I said no.

72
00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.856
You said what?

73
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.976
The reason he was calling was
to make it quite clear that

74
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.616
I would need to be available 24/7.

75
00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.936
And...?

76
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:01.376
And we have two young children.
he knows that.

77
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.736
He knows what you do.

78
00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.816
He made it clear
I could only do the job...

79
00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.480
If you had a good
stay-at-home wifey - right. Yeah.

80
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.216
He said there's a post available
at GCHQ on the China Team

81
00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.456
any time you wanted it.

82
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.536
Less glamorous. more regular.

83
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.760
Excuse me. but he would never ask
a husband to step back for his wife.

84
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.256
I'm not asking you
to give up something you love.

85
00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.376
Yeah. well. I wish I was there

86
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.416
so I could tell him exactly
what I thought of his offer.

87
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.656
DANNY CHUCKLES

88
00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.256
Look. we'll talk. We'll talk.

89
00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.376
I'm sorry. I'm just tired.

90
00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.576
I've been travelling all night

91
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.760
and I've still got to stop
at the Consulate. Mm-hm.

92
00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.496
Well done.

93
00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.056
You are a star...

94
00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.896
CAR RADIO CHATTER
Hang on. hang on.

95
00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.080
NEWS PRESENTER SPEAKS MANDARIN

96
00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.496
Is everything all right? Yeah.

97
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.176
It's fine. just the protests.

98
00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.480
Don't worry.

99
00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.616
Will you kiss the kids for me?
I will.

100
00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.680
Love you. Love you.

101
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.416
NEWS PRESENTER: Hong Kong's
burgeoning Umbrella Revolution

102
00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.816
escalated today

103
00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.176
with further mass demonstrations
on the streets

104
00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.936
as protestors clashed
with Hong Kong police.

105
00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.136
PROTESTORS YELL
Activists say proposed reforms to

106
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.416
the Hong Kong electoral system

107
00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.280
{\an8}would undermine
the democratic process.

108
00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.056
We're very grateful to London

109
00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.680
for sending someone
at such short notice.

110
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.696
President Xi is visiting
the UK next year.

111
00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.536
Leaks detailing our support for
the pro-democracy movements.

112
00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.656
however minimal.

113
00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.016
are proving deeply embarrassing
to the Foreign Office.

114
00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.336
There's nothing in existing
agreements that prohibits it.

115
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.736
Perhaps.

116
00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.096
but we believe these leaks
have led indirectly

117
00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.216
to the arrest of three protestors.
maybe more.

118
00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.096
So we'll need to find
the source of the leaks

119
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.000
or they will close
our HK operation...

120
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.320
and neither of us want that.

121
00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.240
Those of us who grew up out here...

122
00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.760
feel a responsibility.

123
00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.936
Who brought you the leaks?

124
00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.936
A lawyer.

125
00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.576
One of the leaders in
the Occupy Central movement.

126
00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.056
And how do I make contact with them?

127
00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.496
Well. he's asked for a meeting
as soon as you arrived.

128
00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.040
I've taken the liberty
of arranging it.

129
00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.000
Mr Nicky Chan.

130
00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.320
You know him?

131
00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.920
SIREN WAILS

132
00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.840
CHATTER

133
00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:01.760
Bi Ba Ya. You still wear it.

134
00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.256
Well. it's my name.

135
00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.296
The name I gave you.

136
00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.456
Bi - beautiful.

137
00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.536
Ba - precious.

138
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.000
Ya - elegant...

139
00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.360
Barbara.

140
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.360
I took the liberty of ordering.

141
00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.496
Ha!

142
00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.296
Dumplings. of course.

143
00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.280
I mean. we lived off
these as students.

144
00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.440
I can't believe it's you they sent.

145
00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.856
Any thoughts on who's
leaking to the CCP?

146
00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.856
Straight to business.

147
00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.896
I have thoughts -
that's why I flagged it.

148
00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.776
Whoever it is has top access.

149
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.096
Everything we tell your people.
or your people tell us.

150
00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.616
the CCP seem to know immediately.

151
00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.456
But I have no proof.

152
00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.056
Well. hopefully I can help with that.

153
00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.800
{\an8}And you have family now?

154
00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.680
I'm so glad you found someone.

155
00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.440
You? Many.

156
00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.536
No-one like you.

157
00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.880
Ah. don't try and charm me.

158
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.656
You know. you left me
standing in front of that cinema.

159
00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.920
You didn't answer my calls.
you didn't answer my letters.

160
00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.320
Mm. It was wrong.

161
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.120
I should not have behaved like that.

162
00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:34.936
But was I really so bad

163
00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.080
that you had to go and work for
the old colonial enemy in revenge?

164
00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:44.176
I'm here to help you work with
the old colonial enemy

165
00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.656
against the new one.

166
00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.816
"My enemy's enemy." and all that.

167
00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.176
Did you ever think about me?

168
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:53.496
No. Never. NICKY CHUCKLES.

169
00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.656
And even if I tried not to.
your name kept cropping up.

170
00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:00.336
"Nicky Chan. the up-and-coming
star of the Hong Kong bar."

171
00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.016
"Nicky Chan. the human rights hero."

172
00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:04.840
"Nicky Chan. Hong Kong
democracy's great defender."

173
00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:08.280
I'm flattered.

174
00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.080
So...

175
00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.216
do you...?

176
00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.296
Do you have a list of
those you suspect

177
00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.536
of passing information to the CCP?

178
00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.016
The information leaked was
only known by three people -

179
00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.160
two of them my colleagues in
the pro-democracy movement...

180
00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.840
and your guy at the embassy.

181
00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.240
Rupert Wright.

182
00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:39.440
OK.

183
00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.440
OK. let's flush them out.

184
00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:55.760
Right. um...

185
00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.016
I should go.

186
00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.776
Thank you...

187
00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.296
Thank you for the dumplings.

188
00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.360
I've literally been on
the go for 24 hours.

189
00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.360
Right. here...

190
00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.800
tomorrow. lunchtime.

191
00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:14.120
And I'm glad it was you...

192
00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.520
that we had this
chance to meet again.

193
00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.776
Helen Huen? Occupy?

194
00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.296
An Occupy asset. but one of ours.

195
00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.456
Her name has appeared in CCP comms.

196
00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.056
She needs out.

197
00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.600
I'll see what I can do.

198
00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.816
Set a trap. plant some leads.

199
00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.496
then see which one ends up
in the hands of the CCP

200
00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.640
or the Beijing press.

201
00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.440
Then we'll know who our leak is.

202
00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.376
I've taken care of my colleague.

203
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:35.120
Here's a file on two further assets
for each of your two on the list.

204
00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.896
Tell them we're arranging
to get our people out in a hurry

205
00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.496
and then see which one of
the assets' flats is raided.

206
00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.296
What about the assets themselves?

207
00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.320
They're safe.

208
00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:46.960
Already in transit.

209
00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.976
I'm addressing supporters
at the university today -

210
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.416
do you want to come?

211
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.920
Just like the old days.

212
00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:58.720
Don't think I'll fall for that
student leader act again.

213
00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.440
Worth a try.

214
00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.560
PHONE RINGS

215
00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:08.840
Hi. Danny?

216
00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:11.536
It's early there. isn't it?

217
00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.976
Uh. yeah. it's nearly five.

218
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.576
I couldn't sleep.

219
00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:16.600
Is everything OK?

220
00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:19.616
I just. you know.

221
00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.216
I couldn't reach you last night.

222
00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:23.760
and the boys are asking
when you're coming home.

223
00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.496
I tired them out in the park.

224
00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.376
so they're good. They're doing fine.

225
00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.896
They just miss you.

226
00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:32.160
Same as me. I miss you.

227
00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:35.560
I miss you too.

228
00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:41.520
PROTESTORS CHATTER

229
00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.960
PROTESTORS CHANT AND YELL

230
00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.456
DOOR OPENS

231
00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.880
AUDIENCE BOO

232
00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.960
POLICE SPEAK MANDARIN

233
00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.760
No. no. no.

234
00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:17.896
Let me go!

235
00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.016
Leave me be.

236
00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.000
I have diplomatic status -
you can't...

237
00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.656
The Consulate needs to make
an official complaint.

238
00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.936
TV NEWS CHATTER

239
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:36.280
Where's Rupert?

240
00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.240
PHONE RINGS

241
00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.976
Alex. what's going on?

242
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.376
We're getting you out. What?

243
00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.696
What do you mean?

244
00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:49.776
None of you are safe.

245
00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.096
The Hong Kong Police searched
the flat of Helen Huen

246
00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:54.776
almost directly after
you planted the story.

247
00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.936
What. Rupert Wright was the leak?

248
00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.336
Always a shock when it's one of us.

249
00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.656
Jesus Christ.
that smug Etonian bastard.

250
00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:03.576
Look. I have to stay.

251
00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.616
Barbara. the mission is complete.

252
00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:07.416
You've found the source of the leak.

253
00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:08.976
And given that he is one of ours.

254
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:12.336
it compromises you and the whole
of the Hong Kong operation.

255
00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.456
I'm heading into the office
now to wind it down.

256
00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.216
MI6 are abandoning
the people of Hong Kong

257
00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:19.576
when they most need British help.

258
00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:21.416
You can't just leave them to the CCP.

259
00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:22.776
I mean. we have an obligation...

260
00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:24.136
We got our man. Barbara.

261
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.656
You got our man. sadly.

262
00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:29.520
Console yourself with that.
HANGS UP PHONE.

263
00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.880
PHONE BUZZES

264
00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.176
Barbara?

265
00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.096
Danny. can you talk?

266
00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.496
Yeah. sure. What's happening?

267
00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.976
What's going on?

268
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.416
You have to take it.

269
00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.616
What? The job.

270
00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:47.640
Are you crying?

271
00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.176
Maybe.

272
00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.176
You take the job. and I will take
the China Team job. and...

273
00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.400
Are you sure you're all right?

274
00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:56.680
Yeah.

275
00:16:58.680 --> 00:16:59.880
I love you.

276
00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.560
I love... HANGS UP PHONE.

277
00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:12.840
And Nicky Chan?

278
00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.056
The last I saw of him.

279
00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.736
he was being hauled off
by the People's Police.

280
00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.800
God knows where he is now.

281
00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.480
Dr Napier. welcome to GCHQ.

282
00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.920
SIREN WAILS

283
00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:43.496
As we can see from these recent
clips taken on mobile phones.

284
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.376
they had to be smuggled
out of the country.

285
00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:51.256
In short. national security
is being used to wage war

286
00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:54.160
on Hong Kong civil society.

287
00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.136
You are welcome. Dr Napier.

288
00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.296
Dr Barbara Napier.
China Team Leader. GCHQ.

289
00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.320
Sorry I'm late. No problem.

290
00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.176
Thank you for the
first-hand testimony. Julia.

291
00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:13.056
A late addition to today's seminar.

292
00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:16.336
and our next speaker from the School
of Oriental and African Studies.

293
00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.536
University of London.

294
00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.696
on the undermining by the
CCP of the Hong Kong judiciary.

295
00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:21.720
Mr Nicky Chan.

296
00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:29.080
Thank you. Mr Chairman.

297
00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.616
My life had become impossible.

298
00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.176
The state was watching
my every move.

299
00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.736
clients were afraid to approach me.

300
00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.016
people were afraid
to be seen with me.

301
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.040
I had to get out.

302
00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:49.336
I was very fortunate the School
of Oriental and African Studies

303
00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:51.016
offered me a guest lectureship.

304
00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:54.776
I can do more to help
the Hong Kong opposition

305
00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.976
and dissidents of the regime here.

306
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.016
by telling the world.

307
00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.736
or at least whoever will listen.

308
00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.216
what's going on there.

309
00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.936
How long have you been here?
A few months.

310
00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:08.560
And you didn't get in touch?

311
00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:10.880
You have your life.

312
00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:13.160
You should have.

313
00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:16.160
I didn't know what
had happened to you.

314
00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.416
I saw you speak that day.

315
00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.400
I saw you arrested.

316
00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.320
Did they mistreat you?

317
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.040
No worse than others.

318
00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.896
And you?

319
00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.136
You're no longer with Her
Majesty's Secret Service?

320
00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.160
Oh...

321
00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.280
we parted company.

322
00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:41.960
Difference of opinion -
over Hong Kong. in fact.

323
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.000
What?

324
00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.240
Sometimes I think
I made a mistake...

325
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.640
not showing up at
the cinema that night.

326
00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:02.280
25 years I've had to wonder. "Why?"

327
00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.600
"Why did I walk out on the
one woman I ever loved?"

328
00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:10.000
Well. why did you?

329
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:16.800
Do you remember when I finally
took you to see my parents...

330
00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.296
and you charged on ahead
to shake my mother's hand

331
00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.736
while I was struggling up the stairs

332
00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.560
carrying all those
bags and flowers and...?

333
00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.600
You know what my mother said
to me in the kitchen? What?

334
00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.680
She said I looked like your coolie.

335
00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.400
I am so sorry. Barbara.

336
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.600
I beg you to forgive me.

337
00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.320
Oh!

338
00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.560
Of course I forgive you!
It's water under the bridge.

339
00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.280
But. um...

340
00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:15.520
I have to go.

341
00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:23.840
That is very generous of you.

342
00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.736
I hope that
we can be friends at least.

343
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.056
while I am in exile here.

344
00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.080
Of course.

345
00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:32.880
And...

346
00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.520
if I can help your
situation in any way...

347
00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.496
OK. that's great.

348
00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:54.776
I believe I will be seeing
you all in two weeks. OK?

349
00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:56.056
Thank you. guys.

350
00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.456
OK. well. just do me a favour -

351
00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:58.560
just run it again...

352
00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:00.800
just to be sure. Yeah.

353
00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:04.280
Let me call you back.

354
00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.096
What brings you up here?

355
00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.416
I couldn't possibly say.

356
00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.376
The China Nuclear Enquiry.

357
00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:13.696
Uh...

358
00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:16.536
I can neither confirm nor deny.
DANNY CHUCKLES.

359
00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:20.080
So did tricky Dicky Marston take
a brown envelope from the Chinese?

360
00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:24.120
I thought you were going into
London to see an academic friend?

361
00:22:25.120 --> 00:22:26.776
Yeah. Yeah. I've got to go.

362
00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:29.376
Don't forget the boys
have rugby today. OK.

363
00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:30.720
Yep. I'll see you. See you later.

364
00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:36.960
SIREN WAILS

365
00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:51.760
Come in.

366
00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:55.200
Hello?

367
00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:58.776
Not interrupting. am I?

368
00:22:58.800 --> 00:22:59.856
No. not at all.

369
00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:01.456
Seminar over. Ah.

370
00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:02.600
Please. have a seat.

371
00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:08.120
Your paper on the suppression
of Occupy. you know...

372
00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:10.720
it is very powerful.

373
00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:13.456
I only have a few comments.

374
00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:15.096
Always straight to business.

375
00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:17.976
First. what can I get you?
Coffee? Tea?

376
00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:20.176
Um. a glass of water would be fine.

377
00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:21.200
Two ticks.

378
00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:23.920
DOOR OPENS

379
00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:29.960
DOOR CLOSES

380
00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:44.480
DOOR OPENS

381
00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:49.000
Once a spy. always a spy.

382
00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:53.480
DOOR CLOSES What's this?

383
00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:56.960
Pinned to my door this morning.

384
00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:00.336
And it doesn't upset you?

385
00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:02.456
Yes. a bit.

386
00:24:02.480 --> 00:24:04.096
You get used to it.

387
00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:06.176
I mean. Nicky. this is awful.

388
00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:10.816
"Spy. Traitor. CCP stooge."

389
00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:13.096
There are libel laws in this country.

390
00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:15.000
Look at my deleted email file.

391
00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:20.256
There are ways of tracking down
the people who sent these -

392
00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:21.600
my husband would know.

393
00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:24.480
Let's get a drink.

394
00:24:26.200 --> 00:24:27.856
It is a bit early. isn't it?

395
00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:29.536
It's cocktail hour in Hong Kong.

396
00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:31.840
CHATTER

397
00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.976
You know. you should report it.

398
00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.696
Let it go.

399
00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:37.936
Let it go?

400
00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:38.960
You can't.

401
00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:44.200
Nicky. it's a clear CCP campaign
to destroy your credibility.

402
00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:51.896
It comes with the territory.

403
00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:56.176
Yes. and finding and stopping
these people comes with it too.

404
00:24:56.200 --> 00:24:57.736
I know who they are -

405
00:24:57.760 --> 00:24:59.856
Hong Kong students.

406
00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:02.096
One threw eggs at me
coming out of a lecture last week.

407
00:25:02.120 --> 00:25:03.896
Well. I hope the college
did something. Ha!

408
00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:05.816
The students have been radicalised.

409
00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:07.856
They think that non-violent
protesters like me

410
00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:09.336
are a waste of space.

411
00:25:09.360 --> 00:25:12.656
that we've achieved nothing
with decades of peaceful protest.

412
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.456
But violence will lose you
international sympathy.

413
00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:16.616
Exactly.

414
00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:19.816
and that is the mistake that
those who radicalised them

415
00:25:19.840 --> 00:25:21.536
want them to make.

416
00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:22.560
And who's that?

417
00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:25.560
The CCP.

418
00:25:27.200 --> 00:25:30.536
Covertly. of course.
to discredit our movement.

419
00:25:30.560 --> 00:25:34.696
If they can convince the British
government that I am a CCP spy.

420
00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:37.816
I'll be deported and sent
straight to a re-education camp.

421
00:25:37.840 --> 00:25:40.256
But who would believe them?
You hate the CCP.

422
00:25:40.280 --> 00:25:42.656
You've spent your whole life
opposing them.

423
00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:44.120
Sure. but...

424
00:25:45.520 --> 00:25:47.176
they are very smart.

425
00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:50.656
I bet some of your guys
down at GCHQ believe them.

426
00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:51.760
Oh. come on.

427
00:25:52.920 --> 00:25:54.856
I bet. if you look in your files.

428
00:25:54.880 --> 00:25:58.176
you'll find me named as a CCP spy
in intercepted messages.

429
00:25:58.200 --> 00:25:59.616
I know you can't tell me.

430
00:25:59.640 --> 00:26:00.976
but I wouldn't be at all surprised.

431
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.576
Correct. I can't tell you.

432
00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:04.440
And I wouldn't want you to.

433
00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:08.640
And for the moment.
I'm here with you and I'm OK.

434
00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:12.176
Whisky? No.

435
00:26:12.200 --> 00:26:13.200
Sparkling water.

436
00:28:28.760 --> 00:28:29.760
You were right...

437
00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:33.536
the CCP are trying to frame you.

438
00:28:33.560 --> 00:28:35.976
They even photoshopped
you into a picture

439
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:37.856
outside a Croydon Chinese takeaway.

440
00:28:37.880 --> 00:28:40.136
We know it's an overseas
Chinese police station.

441
00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:41.560
So I AM in your files?

442
00:28:43.240 --> 00:28:44.456
Were.

443
00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:45.920
I've taken care of it...

444
00:28:47.040 --> 00:28:48.256
permanently.

445
00:28:48.280 --> 00:28:51.456
Barbara. you're taking
a terrible risk.

446
00:28:51.480 --> 00:28:53.800
I believe one should do
what one knows to be right.

447
00:28:56.640 --> 00:28:58.616
You know. our government
have only ever

448
00:28:58.640 --> 00:29:02.096
exploited and then abandoned
Hong Kong and its people.

449
00:29:02.120 --> 00:29:05.840
I'm not going to be party to the CCP
screwing you all over again.

450
00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:13.160
I owe it to you.

451
00:29:15.520 --> 00:29:17.560
We owe it to Hong Kong.

452
00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:24.560
NICKY EXHALES What is it?

453
00:29:27.120 --> 00:29:28.280
What is it? Are you OK?

454
00:29:30.240 --> 00:29:31.240
Nicky?

455
00:29:32.920 --> 00:29:34.016
Let's walk.

456
00:29:34.040 --> 00:29:35.560
No. no. No. no. no. no.

457
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:38.680
What is it?

458
00:29:41.240 --> 00:29:42.600
I need to tell you a story...

459
00:29:44.800 --> 00:29:45.800
about a boy...

460
00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:48.640
taught to hate his own culture...

461
00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:53.320
to grieve for the end
of colonial rule.

462
00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:58.536
And it took a beautiful.
elegant and precious white woman

463
00:29:58.560 --> 00:30:01.840
to show him the absurdity of
his colonial upbringing.

464
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.576
I've spent the last 25 years

465
00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:07.056
wondering what went wrong
between us. Barbara.

466
00:30:07.080 --> 00:30:11.016
Our relationship was always
going to be unequal.

467
00:30:11.040 --> 00:30:13.640
just like the relationship
between China and the West.

468
00:30:15.800 --> 00:30:18.680
For God's sake. Nicky.
that sounds like CCP talk.

469
00:30:20.080 --> 00:30:21.080
You...

470
00:30:27.720 --> 00:30:28.720
Nicky?

471
00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:36.640
Jesus. Nicky.

472
00:30:38.760 --> 00:30:40.240
Nicky. tell me that you're not...

473
00:30:43.840 --> 00:30:44.840
What?!

474
00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:48.176
W...?

475
00:30:48.200 --> 00:30:49.856
When did they get to you?

476
00:30:49.880 --> 00:30:51.336
When you were arrested?

477
00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:53.120
What. did they torture you?
Is that how?

478
00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:55.600
Before.

479
00:30:57.720 --> 00:31:00.280
Before? But you were working for us.

480
00:31:01.840 --> 00:31:05.136
No. I saw you at the protest.
what you were saying.

481
00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:06.640
You were arrested. and you...

482
00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:13.480
POLICE SPEAK MANDARIN

483
00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:25.000
You were the one that reported
the leak to the Consulate.

484
00:31:31.520 --> 00:31:32.800
You set the trap.

485
00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:37.376
You wanted them to send me.

486
00:31:37.400 --> 00:31:39.840
No. that was just luck.

487
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:45.496
MI6 were getting close to
discovering I was the MSS agent.

488
00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:49.136
Rupert had a lot of
middle-class guilt. like you.

489
00:31:49.160 --> 00:31:50.736
and a Chinese boyfriend -

490
00:31:50.760 --> 00:31:52.400
that's how we turned him.

491
00:31:55.720 --> 00:31:58.496
If you want to protect yourself
and your boyfriend.

492
00:31:58.520 --> 00:32:00.200
you'll need to take the fall.

493
00:32:02.080 --> 00:32:04.440
We persuaded Rupert in return
for looking after them.

494
00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:10.760
"Looking after them..."

495
00:32:14.240 --> 00:32:16.896
After he's served his 14 years.

496
00:32:16.920 --> 00:32:19.976
That's the UK's punishment
for breaking official secrets.

497
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.376
not ours.

498
00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:24.096
I'm sorry you had to
find out this way. truly.

499
00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:26.016
but you need to try to think

500
00:32:26.040 --> 00:32:28.736
beyond all the propaganda
that you've been fed.

501
00:32:28.760 --> 00:32:30.960
The CCP is a responsible power.

502
00:32:32.120 --> 00:32:33.120
China is not Russia.

503
00:32:34.320 --> 00:32:35.840
We are not out to
undermine the West.

504
00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:40.680
You used to say you wanted
to do what is fair and just.

505
00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:44.760
Now is your opportunity.

506
00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:48.520
What?

507
00:32:50.560 --> 00:32:52.640
What. you want me to do
something for you?

508
00:32:55.600 --> 00:32:56.920
Are you out of your mind?

509
00:32:58.400 --> 00:33:01.080
Are you out of your fucking mind?
No. no. no.

510
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.576
I only erased your files

511
00:33:04.600 --> 00:33:07.480
because I believed in what
I thought you stood for.

512
00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:12.720
Jesus Christ.
this has all been a set-up...

513
00:33:14.320 --> 00:33:16.520
the hate mails. the email. Fuck!

514
00:33:18.600 --> 00:33:21.760
You've been playing me ever since
I arrived back in Hong Kong.

515
00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:24.696
SHAKILY: I should have seen.

516
00:33:24.720 --> 00:33:26.440
You saw what you wanted to see.

517
00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:30.656
If this were to come to light.

518
00:33:30.680 --> 00:33:32.480
I'd have to disappear. but you...

519
00:33:33.760 --> 00:33:36.256
you'd lose your job. go to jail.

520
00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:37.440
and the worst part...

521
00:33:38.840 --> 00:33:40.736
your husband.

522
00:33:40.760 --> 00:33:43.496
the new Director of
Operations at GCHQ.

523
00:33:43.520 --> 00:33:45.440
his career would be destroyed...

524
00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:49.080
and so. I imagine.
would your marriage.

525
00:34:51.440 --> 00:34:52.440
Hiya!

526
00:35:00.320 --> 00:35:01.400
Is that you. Barb?

527
00:35:12.960 --> 00:35:13.960
Hello?

528
00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:18.600
Hey.

529
00:35:21.200 --> 00:35:22.480
Barbara. what's wrong?

530
00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:25.400
Hey. what's up?

531
00:35:34.760 --> 00:35:36.200
I want a divorce.

532
00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:42.960
This is a joke. right?

533
00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:49.320
Why on earth...?

534
00:35:51.080 --> 00:35:52.280
Where's this coming from?

535
00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:55.200
I just. um...

536
00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:04.096
It's me. I know. it's me.

537
00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:07.736
I haven't been around much
since I've been Director.

538
00:36:07.760 --> 00:36:09.256
but. no. it's true.

539
00:36:09.280 --> 00:36:11.936
It's true -
you've given up so much for me

540
00:36:11.960 --> 00:36:14.176
and you miss it. you know?

541
00:36:14.200 --> 00:36:15.736
I'll... I'll resign.

542
00:36:15.760 --> 00:36:17.376
No. you've only just been promoted.

543
00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:19.360
You can't resign. I won't let you.

544
00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:22.560
You'd sooner divorce me?

545
00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:26.560
I'm resigning tomorrow.

546
00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:28.600
What?

547
00:36:30.400 --> 00:36:32.200
What is happening?

548
00:36:35.200 --> 00:36:36.200
It's me.

549
00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:43.360
BARBARA BREATHES SHAKILY

550
00:36:49.880 --> 00:36:52.560
I'm so sorry. Danny.

551
00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:57.080
WHISPERS: I'm doing
this to save you...

552
00:36:58.280 --> 00:36:59.280
from me.

553
00:37:04.720 --> 00:37:05.720
I just...

554
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:11.360
I just need a divorce.

555
00:37:12.840 --> 00:37:16.080
OK. OK. OK. OK. Look. just...

556
00:37:17.360 --> 00:37:21.360
If you can look me in the eyes and
tell me that you don't love me...

557
00:37:22.600 --> 00:37:24.040
VOICE TREMBLES: I will let you go.

558
00:37:25.960 --> 00:37:29.816
BARBARA SOBS SOFTLY

559
00:37:29.840 --> 00:37:33.120
Tell me you don't love me.

560
00:37:40.840 --> 00:37:41.840
I love you.

561
00:37:59.440 --> 00:38:00.776
One thing.

562
00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:02.216
You said one thing.

563
00:38:02.240 --> 00:38:03.600
This is the one thing.

564
00:38:05.440 --> 00:38:08.080
We need the MAC address
of a sandbox in Malware.

565
00:38:09.440 --> 00:38:11.840
We launched a ransomware attack
on the NHS.

566
00:38:13.080 --> 00:38:14.560
It will land in Malware
sometime soon.

567
00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:17.320
It contains some Mandarin text.

568
00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:19.760
They'll call your department.

569
00:38:22.040 --> 00:38:23.040
What do you think?

570
00:38:24.920 --> 00:38:26.840
I think it's a lot of Chinese text.

571
00:38:28.800 --> 00:38:30.400
In coding terms. it's nonsense.

572
00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:33.480
What's their game?

573
00:38:34.760 --> 00:38:35.760
Don't know.

574
00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:38.440
I'll call the linguists.

575
00:38:46.760 --> 00:38:48.456
What have you got for me?

576
00:38:48.480 --> 00:38:49.680
It's Phil. isn't it?

577
00:38:51.400 --> 00:38:53.536
Dr Napier. Oh. Barbara. please.

578
00:38:53.560 --> 00:38:55.080
Max said you've got some text.

579
00:38:56.640 --> 00:38:58.496
Yeah. It looks like rubbish.

580
00:38:58.520 --> 00:39:02.096
Uh. not sure I needed
the head of department.

581
00:39:02.120 --> 00:39:03.936
Well. I need to keep my hand in.

582
00:39:03.960 --> 00:39:05.736
do my share of the grunt work.

583
00:39:05.760 --> 00:39:06.760
Yeah.

584
00:39:08.360 --> 00:39:09.360
Right.

585
00:39:14.200 --> 00:39:16.376
But I did miss my morning coffee.

586
00:39:16.400 --> 00:39:19.056
I don't think I can do
this without caffeine.

587
00:39:19.080 --> 00:39:22.816
You wouldn't be an angel and get me a
latte from the coffee van. would you?

588
00:39:22.840 --> 00:39:23.960
Here.

589
00:39:27.280 --> 00:39:28.280
Have one yourself.

590
00:39:31.200 --> 00:39:32.720
For the boss's wife. I guess.

591
00:39:34.080 --> 00:39:35.080
Thank you.

592
00:40:21.680 --> 00:40:22.976
Ah.

593
00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:25.496
Sorry. just too much Chinese slang.

594
00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:27.616
Calvin. however. is all over it -

595
00:40:27.640 --> 00:40:29.120
cousins in Beijing.

596
00:40:31.680 --> 00:40:33.680
Right. I'll leave you to it.

597
00:40:38.400 --> 00:40:39.400
Barbara?

598
00:40:43.720 --> 00:40:44.720
Yeah?

599
00:40:45.920 --> 00:40:46.920
Your coffee.

600
00:40:48.280 --> 00:40:49.360
Oh. of course.

601
00:40:50.560 --> 00:40:51.560
Sorry.

602
00:40:53.200 --> 00:40:54.800
In need of caffeine.

603
00:40:58.360 --> 00:41:00.400
CHATTER

604
00:41:21.960 --> 00:41:22.960
Do you have it?

605
00:41:34.600 --> 00:41:36.200
I have done this one thing.

606
00:41:39.960 --> 00:41:42.320
NECKLACE JINGLES

607
00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:45.640
Now I never...

608
00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:49.640
ever want to see you again.

609
00:42:02.480 --> 00:42:03.800
I never wanted to hurt you.

610
00:42:13.720 --> 00:42:15.480
I have somewhere else I need to be.

611
00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:21.160
Hey.

612
00:43:23.080 --> 00:43:24.280
You got back in time.

613
00:43:26.280 --> 00:43:27.496
Yeah.

614
00:43:27.520 --> 00:43:29.440
Well. it's our anniversary.

615
00:43:32.720 --> 00:43:34.320
What happened to your necklace?

616
00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:37.840
I. um...

617
00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:40.160
I got rid of it.

618
00:43:42.040 --> 00:43:44.416
Consigned the past to the past.

619
00:43:44.440 --> 00:43:48.216
Criminals always return
to the scene of the crime.

620
00:43:48.240 --> 00:43:50.560
LAUGHTER

621
00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:52.640
You all right? Mm.

622
00:43:53.880 --> 00:43:55.136
Hello. you. Hey.

623
00:43:55.160 --> 00:43:56.440
How are you? Yeah.

624
00:43:58.800 --> 00:44:01.280
Happy "When Danny Met Barbara" Day.
you two.

625
00:44:02.840 --> 00:44:04.296
Everything all right. guys?

626
00:44:04.320 --> 00:44:06.696
Yeah. everything's all right.

627
00:44:06.720 --> 00:44:07.920
All good.

628
00:44:09.920 --> 00:44:11.656
Well. whatever it is.

629
00:44:11.680 --> 00:44:15.240
tonight. we leave home at home
and work at work.

630
00:44:17.600 --> 00:44:18.856
Your usual - I took the liberty.

631
00:44:18.880 --> 00:44:21.056
LAUGHTER Ah. thank you. Ravi.

632
00:44:21.080 --> 00:44:22.496
Ms Napier.

633
00:44:22.520 --> 00:44:24.016
Thank you.

634
00:44:24.040 --> 00:44:25.040
Thanks. Ravi.

635
00:44:26.480 --> 00:44:28.056
Thank you. sir.

636
00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:29.360
I'll take those for you.

637
00:44:32.560 --> 00:44:33.760
Cheers. Cheers.

638
00:44:36.160 --> 00:44:37.160
Cheers.

639
00:44:41.800 --> 00:44:43.240
15 years ago...

640
00:44:44.920 --> 00:44:46.416
on this day.

641
00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:48.576
in this very restaurant.

642
00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:51.656
a nervous young man
was out on a date

643
00:44:51.680 --> 00:44:53.840
with a beautiful MI6 agent...

644
00:44:55.600 --> 00:44:57.120
only for his...

645
00:44:58.280 --> 00:45:01.040
best friend to run into them
and run off with the girl.

646
00:45:02.960 --> 00:45:05.856
Married her. last I heard.
Innocent. Your Honour.

647
00:45:05.880 --> 00:45:09.176
I only stopped by to pick up
a chicken tikka masala.

648
00:45:09.200 --> 00:45:10.800
You asked me over.

649
00:45:12.440 --> 00:45:13.456
Yeah.

650
00:45:13.480 --> 00:45:14.960
To be fair.
it wasn't going very well.

651
00:45:17.160 --> 00:45:20.296
And when you brought him over.
I looked up.

652
00:45:20.320 --> 00:45:22.216
There you were. in your anorak.

653
00:45:22.240 --> 00:45:23.616
It was a jacket. Yeah. mm-hm.

654
00:45:23.640 --> 00:45:25.000
Jacket. OK.

655
00:45:26.200 --> 00:45:29.240
And when I looked up. I thought...

656
00:45:30.840 --> 00:45:32.600
"Who is this beautiful man..."

657
00:45:34.680 --> 00:45:36.880
"Who I want to spend
the rest of my life with?"

658
00:45:49.840 --> 00:45:51.136
Are you all right?

659
00:45:51.160 --> 00:45:52.800
Yeah. Yeah. I. um...

660
00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:57.496
I'm just going to nip
to the bathroom.

661
00:45:57.520 --> 00:45:58.680
I'll be two secs.

662
00:46:58.320 --> 00:46:59.840
SHE CLEARS THROAT

